e with any external parties  and we set up specific role based access  controls even within our organization  such as only granting the public cloud  engineering team and reliable  engineering team to access to manage  compute engines  we mandated security keys and 10-minute  session timeouts for our super admins as  you can imagine those a very powerful  accountant we want to protect them  accordingly  we also took a step where we blocked  virtual machine images from being shared  between projects because this was  another control for us to prevent the  exfiltration of my data from potentially  a more secure production environment to  a development environment that's less  lockdown finally we use V PC service  controls and specifically the security  parameters product to protect data in  locations such as Google Cloud storage  and bigquery at the API level these  policies together let us secure access  to our resources and they're pretty easy  for us to edit and iterate on as we  implement additional policies or as we  decide to change our security model so  that secures the users and some of the  data but what about the network all of  our virtual machines are launched in  virtual private cloud environments and  this helps keep them segmented and  segregated at the network level we use  organization policies and firewall rules  to limit access from anything outside of  the V PC to hitting those hosts of  course we had to connect the V pcs to  data sources in our internal data  centers to enable kind of research  workflows and modeling and we use  private inter connect to do that this  communication also enabled accessibility  to our internal Kerberos infrastructure  so we use that to handle system  authentication and authorization at the  operating system layer the same way we  would on frame gives us a unified  authorization model to further lock  things down in all of our V pcs we  remove the write to the internet so that  no external resources can be accessed  